        <mxCell id="repCache" value="replication" style="endArrow=classic;startArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 4;strokeWidth=2;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="cachePrimary" target="cacheReplica" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="repRds" value="replication" style="endArrow=classic;startArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 4;strokeWidth=2;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="rdsMain" target="rdsStandby" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Z8DqSg6ur86CymlxQR2D-1" value="&lt;b&gt;Request flow – steps 1 to 7&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1 – Users → Internet Gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Phone and web clients send and receive chat traffic (HTTPS / WebSocket) through the Internet Gateway, the entry point of the VPC.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2 – Internet Gateway → Elastic Load Balancer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The gateway passes incoming traffic to the load balancer, which has a node in each public subnet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3 – Load Balancer → Chat servers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The load balancer spreads connections across Chat server 1 (AZ a) and Chat server 2 (AZ b), health-checks them, and relays the responses back to the users.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4 – Chat servers ↔ Distributed cache&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Both servers read and write the cache primary for live message delivery and recent messages. The primary is replicated to the replica in the other AZ.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5 – Chat servers ↔ RDS MySQL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Both servers read and write users, contacts and groups on RDS main. It is replicated to the standby for failover.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6 – Chat servers ↔ DynamoDB&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every message is saved to DynamoDB as permanent message history, and older history is read from it when a user scrolls back.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;7 – Chat servers ↔ Elastic File System&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Both servers store and fetch shared files (attachments, media) on EFS, so a file saved by one server is visible to the other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Sending a message: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (deliver live) → 6 (save history). Opening a chat: 5 (who/which group) → 4 (recent messages) → 6 (older history).&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;labelBackgroundColor=#E5CCFF;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="72" y="781" width="868.5" height="388" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
